            <div xml:id="d527">

                <pb facs="0748" n="646" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg646"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/1086: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-09-09T18:00:00+01:00">September 9,
                            1935—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 9—2:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>293. I have just been informed by an American, in whom I have complete
                    confidence, that he has learned that the propositions presented <pb facs="0749"
                        n="647" xml:id="pg647"/> to the Italians in the recent tripartite
                    conversations at Paris were not transmitted to Ethiopia at the time but only a
                    few days ago; that the Abyssinian representatives here have today received a
                    reply to the effect that the Negus would agree to these propositions as a basis
                    for discussion under two conditions; (1) that the concessions by Ethiopia would
                    not be made to Italy <hi rendition="#italic">qua</hi> Italy but to the League
                    though Italy could profit under them and, (2) that the Negus as a member of the
                    League would have a say in the appointment of the “administrators”.</p>
                <p>So far as my informant is aware the fact[s] of this reply have not yet been
                    communicated to the powers concerned and still remains a secret in the Ethiopian
                    delegation. I am therefore not repeating this telegram anywhere.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
